WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.846
A group records reversible operations and how they combine

00:00:03.846 --> 00:00:08.058
Consider the four rotations of a square that preserve its position

00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:14.567
Doing a quarter turn and then another quarter turn has the same effect as one half turn.

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:20.130
Label those rotations zero, one, two, and three quarter turns

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.261
Composition becomes addition modulo four

00:00:22.261 --> 00:00:24.393
Zero acts as the identity

00:00:24.393 --> 00:00:32.067
Three quarter turns undo one quarter turn, because together they make a full turn back to the start.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:38.778
The group axioms require closure, an identity, inverses, and associativity

00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:42.567
Associativity changes parentheses while keeping operation order

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:51.767
It follows here from composing rotations, or from integer addition before reducing the resulting remainder modulo four.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:56.081
A half turn is its own inverse

00:00:56.081 --> 00:01:01.679
These four rotations also commute, but commutativity is not a general group axiom

00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:09.000
Rotations and reflections together form a larger symmetry group where swapping operation order can change the result.
